name: sim.handleDistance
description: 
luaSynopsis: int result,float smallestDistance=sim.handleDistance(int distanceObjectHandle)
inputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. distanceObjectHandle: handle of the distance object or sim.handle_all or sim.handle_all_except_explicit. (sim.handle_all will handle all registered distance objects, while sim.handle_all_except_explicit will only handle those that are not marked as "explicit handling")
2. smallestDistance: smallest measured distance. Can be nullptr
outputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. result: 1 if at least one distance was measured, 0 if no distance was measured
2. smallestDistance: the smallest distance measured.
